    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an e15 error code and won't start. i looked at the manual but it's kind of confusing. can u tell me how to check the leak sensor and how to actually dry out the base of the machine properly?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To check the leak sensor, unplug the Bosch dishwasher from power and carefully locate the leak sensor, usually a small plastic valve or holder near the door seals. Gently wiggle or rotate the sensor while observing for any signs of proper function, such as water flowing freely. If it sticks or clogs, clean or replace it according to the manual instructions. \n\nFor drying out the machine base, allow the dishwasher to air dry completely after each use. If the issue persists, use a soft cloth to gently dry the base, paying particular attention to any areas around the door seals and drain hose connections. Avoid touching electrical components or exposing the machine to excessive water.",
